From 9c35150ee5acd35d80ea8f76c368faab3ed531dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Creitin Gameplays <clton999@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 23:42:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/17] diag: setup/initcall checkpoint selectors,
 LF-normalized scripts

prepare_stage_panics.py gains a checkpoint selector (setup:<name> or
initcall:<level>:<name|ordinal>) that writes a breadcrumb and requests a
direct PSCI SYSTEM_RESET before the selected setup step or initcall;
stage_build.sh passes it through with an explicit smc/hvc conduit choice.
The generated diag_stage.h snapshot and the init/main.c hooks are
regenerated with every knob off (panic=0 arm=0 smc=0 checkpoint=off
paint=0 screen=0).

The scripts are LF-normalized: a CRLF copy synced from a Windows host
made bash reject "set -eo pipefail" on this machine.
---
